    "done_when": "Per §79 of the plan: needs_you.needs_you_runs reads a run's deferral through the reader the obligations view uses, obligations._acknowledgements_in_force, without editing reckon/crew/obligations.py (a peer holds it), leaves the run out until the deferral's instant, and lets it return once, as a change, when the deferral expires. A test in a temporary home finds a delivered run deferred an hour ahead not named, named once at the deferral plus one second, and a run with an expired deferral named. If obligations.py must change, stop with status blocked and say why. Every test file importing the changed modules, rebuilt from the head tree, adds no failure against a base arm, both arms from git checkouts under the run's own scratch directory with RECKON_SESSION_HOST_SETTLE, RECKON_FOLLOWER_OWNER, RECKON_FOLLOWER_IMAGE_COMMIT and RECKON_FOLLOWER_SOURCE_ROOT unset, run in place on the fleet node with pytest -n 8; any id failing in one arm only is run five times alone in each arm. tests/test_every_module_fits_a_worker_window.py passes at head. Every log is under the run directory, starts with its revision and the literal command, and ends in EXIT=. ruff check and ruff format --check add no findings on the changed files, judged against the base blobs.",
